      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5604,
      "endIndex": 5634,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_3",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Leila's Tango Club Experience",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00072",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[72]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 5634,
      "endIndex": 6168,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Leila discussed her experience with the tango club, explaining that she initially attended lessons as a freshman but found the diverse age groups uncomfortable. She returned later in her freshman year and discovered she enjoyed tango. Leila eventually joined the club's leadership as vice president in her sophomore year after the graduating seniors asked for help. Most effective recruitment channel for leadership team: Direct personal appeals to join the leadership team by current leaders as well as volunteers asking to do more.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00073",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[73]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6168,
      "endIndex": 6169,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00074",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[74]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6169,
      "endIndex": 6210,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_3",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Student Dance Club Leadership Transition",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00075",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[75]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6210,
      "endIndex": 6458,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Dan and Leila discussed the leadership transition of a student dance club, particularly focusing on the Tango Club at Stanford. Leila explained that her motivation to take on leadership came from wanting to help after being inspired by the tango. ",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00076",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[76]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6458,
      "endIndex": 6459,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00077",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[77]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6459,
      "endIndex": 6493,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_3",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Dance Club Recruitment Strategies",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00078",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[78]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6493,
      "endIndex": 6961,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Leila explained that while dance clubs face challenges in recruiting students due to time constraints, they naturally attract interest through club fairs and social media channels. She noted that email is the most effective communication channel, though the club also uses Instagram and the cards system run by the Associated Students. Leila mentioned that students often sign up for their mailing list and follow their Instagram without specific advertising to them.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00079",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[79]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6961,
      "endIndex": 6962,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00080",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[80]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6962,
      "endIndex": 6997,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_3",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Student Recruitment for Tango Club",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00081",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[81]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 6997,
      "endIndex": 7644,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Leila explained that student recruitment for their tango club primarily happens through ASSU announcements and club fairs at the beginning of the year, with the undergrad club fair scheduled for September 30th to October 2nd and the grad club fair on September 18th. She mentioned that Richard Powers' dance classes, which attract 60-70 students each, are also effective recruitment channels, with opportunities to place flyers and make announcements during class. When asked about relevance for other dance styles like Bachata, Leila indicated that Bachata would likely be appropriate since it's similar to what Powers teaches in Social Dance 1.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00082",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[82]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 7644,
      "endIndex": 7675,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_3",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Tango Class Promotion Strategy",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00083",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[83]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 7675,
      "endIndex": 8156,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Leila discussed the promotion of tango classes at Stanford Ballroom, mentioning that they currently teach basic bachata moves and have offered classes at Dance Break. She highlighted the success of their performances at the Viennese Ball, which helped showcase the potential of tango to a wider audience. Leila noted that while they have a core group of dedicated dancers, there is no specific incentive for students to continue beyond basic lessons, making retention a challenge.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00084",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[84]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 8156,
      "endIndex": 8192,
      "namedStyleType": "HEADING_3",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "University Dance Space Reservations",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00085",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[85]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
      "segmentId": null,
      "startIndex": 8192,
      "endIndex": 8665,
      "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "isListItem": false,
      "listId": null,
      "nestingLevel": null,
      "table": null,
      "text": "Leila explained the process for reserving university spaces for dance activities, including options like EBGR studios, Havana Room, Kennedy grad room, Robley studios through the Department of Theater and Performance Studies, and EPC. She noted specific rules and quotas for different spaces, such as the two-week advance reservation limit at EPC and the twice-a-quarter limit at the Havana room. Leila also mentioned that Koret is the only space where payment is required.",
      "protectedControls": []
    },
    {
      "paragraphId": "P00086",
      "path": "tabs.t.0.body.content[86]",
      "tabId": "t.0",
      "tabTitle": "Tab 1",
